The quotations, with their sections and pages, are in `docs/standards.md`. The table says what the controls cover, nothing more.

| Expectation | What valiwatt does | Where it is checked |
|---|---|---|
| SR 11-7, conceptual soundness, including sensitivity analysis | Model, input and decision rule fixed in the plan before any v2 replay; the GAM's curves shown beside a fit without the lags. Alternative specifications: v1's form on the forecast, the observed-weather bound, a {{ K.late_h|num(0) }}-hour availability margin, the mean of the {{ dq.sources.eccc|length }} stations, an absolute interval, one quantile per season. These are not the small changes to inputs and parameters SR 11-7 calls sensitivity analysis; those are not made. | v2's plan, sections 4 and 8; the validation and frozen-model runs |
| SR 11-7, data quality and relevance | {{ dq.checks.values()|selectattr('kind', 'equalto', 'gate')|list|length }} quality gates over the whole window, every repair documented; in production, a daily quality monitor on the raw records, a day without a forecast included. | Data-quality report; replays |
| SR 11-7, third-party data and models: NOAA's forecast input | Covered: its quality gates, its availability rule, its error against the observations, its drift and the sensitivity to availability. Not covered: the soundness and change management of NOAA's model itself. | Sections 2 and 8; data-quality report |
| SR 11-7, ongoing monitoring: process verification | Lookahead guards; a clock that refuses later data, forecasts included; the three models' hashes checked before and after; the replay refuses to run if the rules or the dependencies differ from tag `{{ freeze.freeze_tag }}`{% if departures %}; the tag was moved by a departure recorded in `AGENTS.md` (section 8){% endif %}. Each guard has its break. | Section 11 |
| SR 11-7, ongoing monitoring: benchmarking | Two comparison models (v1 as shipped and v1's form on the same forecast), a naive baseline, the observed-weather bound; frozen model against refitted folds on {{ p.year }}. | Sections 3, 7 and 8 |
| SR 11-7, outcomes analysis and back-testing, with intervals | Monthly folds with an embargo; intervals of conformal form whose coverage is measured. {% if not held %}The back-test in SR 11-7's sense is {{ HY }}, held-out data: pending.{% elif not R.finished %}The back-test in SR 11-7's sense is to be {{ HY }}: its test of record started and did not finish, so there is no claim on held-out data.{% elif R.evaluation == 'held_out' and R.standing == 'clean' %}The back-test in SR 11-7's sense is {{ HY }}, held-out data: done, its test of record clean.{% else %}{{ HY }}'s test of record finished, labelled {{ label(R.evaluation) }}, standing "{{ OUTCOME[R.standing] }}": it is not a back-test on held-out data.{% endif %} {{ span(vy) }} served the choice, {{ r.year }} was seen by the developers. | Sections 3, 5, 8 and 9 |
| SR 11-7, acceptability thresholds, then recalibration or redevelopment | Seasonal thresholds drawn from earlier weeks; an ordered decision table, with evidence; v2's decision rule against v1 fixed in advance; recommends without acting. | Sections 1, 6, 8 and 9 |
| SR 11-7, documentation and validation reports | This report and its model card, generated from the runs and stamped with their identifiers and the code hash. | This report |
| NIST MAP 2.2, 2.3 | Intended use, out of scope, weather caveat, limitations; validation plan and data-quality findings documented. | Model card; plan |
| NIST MEASURE 1.1, 2.1, 2.3, 2.5, 2.13 | MLflow runs (test sets, metrics, parameters, versions); replays under production conditions; breaks; the "not covered" list below. | Runs; section 11 |
| NIST MANAGE 2.2 | Weekly recommendations with evidence; who acts, and how, is out of scope. | Section 8 |

**Not covered.** Independent validation and effective challenge (SR 11-7, V; NIST MEASURE 1.3); governance, policies and controls, internal audit, model inventory (SR 11-7, VI; NIST GOVERN for the most part); periodic review; analysis of overrides of the model's outputs; use in decisions and materiality; independent review of a recalibration; sensitivity analysis in SR 11-7's sense; the soundness and change management of NOAA's model; NIST MANAGE 2.4 (who supersedes, disengages or deactivates the model); NIST MANAGE 4.1 and 1.4 beyond the card's limitations; NIST MEASURE 2.4 (monitoring in production: simulated by the replay only); real-time data.

